        "original_id": "bbe07388-24a2-52de-8c3e-ff7cfa24525e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1971 Canadian Grand Prix\n- People: Mark Donohue\n- Places: Mosport Park\n- Topics: Formula One\n\nFacts:\n- The 1971 Canadian Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held at Mosport Park on September 19, 1971.\n- Mark Neary Donohue Jr. was born on March 18, 1937, and died on August 19, 1975.\n- Mark Donohue was an American racecar driver nicknamed \"Captain Nice\" and later \"Dark Monohue.\"\n- Mark Donohue was known for setting up his own race car as well as driving it to victories.\n- American driver Mark Donohue finished third on his Formula One debut at the 1971 Canadian Grand Prix.",
